+# TOON-PATCH 0001 (ToonStudio V12 §5 toon-vello fork track).
+#
+# WHY: wgpu still has no way to build a `wgpu::Device` around a `GPUDevice`
+# the page already owns (`Device::from_custom` demands a whole custom
+# backend rather than adoption). Without adoption, ToonStudio's WGSL filter
+# kernels and vello are forced onto two separate `GPUDevice`s, so every
+# exchange is a CPU readback (V12 §6.3 L0) — measured at 2.9x the same-device
+# GPU copy at 1024² (`tests/benchmarks/results/gpu-fabric-probe.json`).
+#
+# On the 29.0.4 base this patch also backported the *export* half
+# (`Device::as_webgpu`, `Texture::as_webgpu`,
+# `Device::create_texture_from_webgpu_handle`, public `wgpu::webgpu`).
+# wgpu 30 ships all of that upstream, so on this 30.0.1 base the patch is
+# only the *adoption* half: `Device::from_webgpu_handle` plus the
+# `WebDevice`/`WebQueue::from_external_handle` constructors behind it. That
+# half has no upstream counterpart and is our upstream PR candidate
+# (V12 §5.4).
+#
+# OFF BY DEFAULT ON PURPOSE: with this feature disabled, every patch hunk in
+# this vendored tree compiles out and the crate is API-identical to upstream
+# 30.0.1. That is build track A (`upstream`) — it is what detects upstream
+# regressions. Track B (`toon`) enables `toon-fabric`.
+#
+# REMOVE WHEN: wgpu upstream ships `Device`/`Queue` adoption of an external
+# WebGPU handle AND vello's wgpu pin reaches that release.
+toon-fabric = []
 trace = [
